, view, and delete commands. Extend parsing for bare flags and command-specific validation, with tests covering shared state, invalid input, and duplicate tags.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":471,"deletions":52},"other":{"insertions":2,"deletions":2},"test-code":{"insertions":222,"deletions":12}}}]},{"date":"2026-10-09T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"93c20590f072d2b3e3013de4baab24999aa978d6","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #25 from 77chenchen/WangQichen-Aboutus","messageBody":"Add member management commands","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]},{"date":"2026-10-13T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"be365ed919fb10f8d8a902501313373e6736c613","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #27 from 77chenchen/master","messageBody":"Fix welcome banner Checkstyle violations","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"0f9f17d2ad9f7ccda062174d587dedd41cbf7a06","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #26 from Bryan-chua/bryan-save-load","messageBody":"Added commands to save and load club data","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"45f9137ad0dc95598380e7ebb87ec8db8a33ab54","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #28 from AY2627S1-CS2113-W10-2/ui-design","messageBody":"Welcome message UI design","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"aa7b8f6f29983f8c9c943d252874c0f612655c61","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Improve defensive handling and runtime diagnostics","messageBody":"Validate parser, domain, persistence, and command boundaries so invalid state fails clearly. Add invariant assertions, structured logging, and defensive tests while disabling the temporary test command in the application.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":411,"deletions":128},"test-code":{"insertions":70,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"ffae758e52d584615caa1fb4fdd43724f29d7c78","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Route application logs away from console","messageBody":"Configure the clubflow package logger to write diagnostic records to a file without inheriting Java\u0027s console handler. Ignore generated log and lock files so runtime diagnostics do not pollute version control.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":29,"deletions":0}}}]},{"date":"2026-10-21T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"2cd1a7ca040c1e813dbc2ddf6bb51aa09486f389","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Improve event detail display and verify the event command workflow","messageBody":"Use a shared labelled display for both event view modes, show placeholders for missing details, and format budgets consistently with an empty-list message.\n\nAdd six output regression tests and move the shared-data workflow tests into the command package. Verify each view response independently before and after deletion so stale output cannot hide a failure.\n\nValidation: all 32 tests and both Checkstyle checks passed on Java 25.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":34,"deletions":5},"other":{"insertions":58,"deletions":13},"test-code":{"insertions":158,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"68600748a93195f6348a7d26ec77a5df123d08a3","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Expand application and persistence tests and enable run assertions","messageBody":"Add 22 tests for scripted application sessions, startup, invalid-input recovery, persistence round trips and malformed records, and shared-data replacement and member indexing.\n\nRemove the unconditional failing debug assertion that prevented startup with assertions enabled. Enable assertions for the Gradle run task so normal development runs exercise invariant checks.\n\nValidation: all 54 tests and both Checkstyle checks pass on Java 25 with the committed Gradle 9.6.1 and local Gradle 9.7.1.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":0,"deletions":1},"other":{"insertions":1,"deletions":0},"test-code":{"insertions":407,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"3235ee6b0dc54d7df119b5c921ca160b0ce1238c","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add extensible find command for event tags and names","messageBody":"Route find requests through registered search handlers so future search types can be added independently. Implement case-insensitive partial matching for events with argument validation and current-data results.\n\nCover search dispatch and event workflows with tests, and replace template user-guide content with ClubFlow commands and examples.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":129,"deletions":0},"docs":{"insertions":107,"deletions":18},"test-code":{"insertions":222,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"c1dc51b0ca2de12713199f77d8ccb44fd2498199","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add partial event editing while preserving event order","messageBody":"Introduce editEvent with case-insensitive tag selection and updates limited to supplied fields. Replace immutable events at their existing index so list order and prior snapshots are preserved, and validate all supplied values before applying changes.\n\nShare date, budget, and field validation with event creation to keep command rules consistent. Document editing and test partial updates, invalid requests, view/find integration, ordering, and persistence.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":187,"deletions":57},"docs":{"insertions":18,"deletions":1},"test-code":{"insertions":236,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"2f1efa5ea928ffa7f10eb6361acd275edb937fb4","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add extensible mark and unmark commands for event completion","messageBody":"Route completion requests through registered item handlers so future member support can be added independently. Set event completion without toggling repeated requests, preserve immutable snapshots and event order, and retain completion when editing details.\n\nDisplay completion in event views and persist it in save files while loading legacy events as not completed. Document the commands and cover dispatch, validation, repeated requests, editing, ordering, display, and persistence with tests.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":186,"deletions":5},"docs":{"insertions":23,"deletions":1},"test-code":{"insertions":306,"deletions":12}}},{"hash":"08f5ac2badc4010e0cbb75f608e82540a6058b4f","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Cover completion persistence and unknown event deletion workflows","messageBody":"Exercise create, mark, save, load, view, and unmark through complete application sessions to prove completion and event details survive a restart. Use an isolated relative save path and clean up the temporary files.\n\nVerify deleting an unknown tag reports the expected message while preserving existing event objects and their order.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"test-code":{"insertions":59,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"198731ba5a1363f6868ab61beca4859930def4ed","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Centralize missing-event errors through ClubFlowException","messageBody":"Introduce EventNotFoundException for view, edit, delete, mark, and unmark requests and propagate checked application errors through command execution and parsing. Handle them once in the main loop so errors have consistent messages and users can continue entering commands.\n\nReplace completion BiConsumer handlers with a checked-exception-capable CompletionHandler interface while retaining future item-type extensibility. Update tests for exception propagation, unchanged stored events, and application recovery, and document the tagged view error.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":68,"deletions":38},"docs":{"insertions":1,"deletions":0},"test-code":{"insertions":125,"deletions":60}}},{"hash":"2217ce3ef390cbdc9cae5da9cf4b90939313478d","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Handle duplicate event creation through ClubFlowException","messageBody":"Throw DuplicateEventException when createEvent encounters an existing case-insensitive tag so the main loop reports the error consistently and keeps accepting commands. Preserve existing event details, completion state, and list order.\n\nVerify exact and mixed-case duplicate tags, allow identical names with distinct tags, and cover centralized error reporting and recovery in a full application session. Document the duplicate-tag message.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":20,"deletions":5},"docs":{"insertions":1,"deletions":0},"test-code":{"insertions":47,"deletions":5}}}]},{"date":"2026-10-22T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"bf70e4583738ce32f8c4bb21a20e71939cf76f93","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Refactor event editing to clarify replacement construction","messageBody":"Extract supplied-or-original field values into named local variables before constructing the replacement event. Separate parsing and fallback logic from object creation while preserving omitted fields and completion state.\n\nValidation: all 10 EditEventCommandTest tests passed with Java 25.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":14,"deletions":13}}},{"hash":"dc70f2df0f9ee6789add9d674ca06f822828cdcb","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Address review feedback on test names and event indentation","messageBody":"Rename prefix-style test files and classes to the ClassNameTest convention. Add a reusable indentation overload to UserInterface.print and use it for aligned event details, preserving existing output.\n\nValidation: all 99 JUnit tests plus main and test Checkstyle checks passed with Java 25.0.4.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":37,"deletions":9},"other":{"insertions":78,"deletions":75}}}]},{"date":"2026-10-25T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"1059af3f7dffdfa926e685bed5d306ce413e4b04","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #52 from 77chenchen/master","messageBody":"Add member editing, fuzzy search, and event assignments","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]},{"date":"2026-10-26T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"716c83efe785219b22f39a63130bada8922c278e","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #54 from camimaigrot/multiple-clubs","messageBody":"Add support for multiple clubs","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"e4b4a8b4ce91b2dbcbfaf835de4cda94cba9496d","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Refactor event search into FindEventCommand with optional field filters","messageBody":"Separate event searching from member searching with the fe alias. Support name, venue, logistics, general text, and exact date filters combined with AND, while keeping e/ tag-or-name matching optional.\n\nReject empty, blank, and null search arguments; update command help, the UserGuide, and regression tests for the expanded search behavior.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":136,"deletions":81},"docs":{"insertions":17,"deletions":12},"test-code":{"insertions":317,"deletions":212}}},{"hash":"43c54354bef939e9b4c7a24176eaea1bd22f84f6","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add budget and completion-status filters to event search","messageBody":"Allow exact budgets, inclusive minimum/maximum bounds, and completed/pending status to combine with existing filters. Reject non-finite or negative budgets, conflicting bounds, and invalid statuses before searching.\n\nUpdate help and the UserGuide, and add regression coverage for boundaries, validation, data preservation, and mark/unmark integration.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":69,"deletions":4},"docs":{"insertions":10,"deletions":2},"test-code":{"insertions":137,"deletions":10}}}]},{"date":"2026-10-27T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"31e354a8c96a87200bd64a4e6902cd140a252292","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"docs: provide an event-focused developer roadmap","messageBody":"Replace the starter guide with concise navigation, architecture context, and\ndesign decisions for event management and completion. Leave teammate-owned\nsections as headings so the guide can be extended without duplicating code.\n\nInclude reviewed PlantUML sources and rendered diagrams, with label sizing\nmatched to the guide\u0027s body text. Document assignment cleanup on event deletion\nand the boundary between event mutations and autosave.\n\nValidation: 53 event command tests passed on Java 25; the isolated CLI walkthrough\nverified restart persistence and assignment cleanup; rendered previews, links,\nand whitespace checks passed.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":547,"deletions":19}}},{"hash":"62bbbfaa46320f266f2f928f6554b148bffc6154","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"chore: identify event feature and test contributions","messageBody":"Add author boundaries around event workflows and their supporting tests so\ncontribution ownership is traceable without changing application behavior.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":30,"deletions":3},"test-code":{"insertions":19,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"37ab58d8f82f92008ffdd209d40d58e689f45ff7","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #56 from Bryan-chua/bryan-autocorrect","messageBody":"implemented autocorrect feature + added test scripts","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]}],"77chenchen":[{"date":"2026-09-30T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"ab8ad8ef8fdabc11178ebb481250fb5f6753ddc2","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"changing about AboutUS.md","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":1,"deletions":5}}},{"hash":"bcd7475fdd6c6b279373758cee6cd85202cdf907","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027master\u0027 of https://github.com/AY2627S1-CS2113-W10-2/tp into WangQichen-Aboutus","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"a82f21682aa9067eb2596c52df4906926bb6a746","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027master\u0027 of https://github.com/AY2627S1-CS2113-W10-2/tp into WangQichen-Aboutus","messageBody":"","fileT